## Drawers

@narrator{code="0010"}: Twenty-four drawers, numbered in brass. Frost has grown over the handles like mould.
<branch id="drawer" prompt="Which drawer?">
  <choice id="seven" label="Drawer 7">
    @narrator{code="0020"}: A hand. Grey, patient, palm up, as if waiting to be given something.
    @nell{code="0010"}: Sorry. Sorry.
    ::fright{amount=2}
  </choice>
  <choice id="twentyOne" label="Drawer 21">
    @narrator{code="0030"}: Empty. The runners scream all the way out and all the way back.
    ::lure{room="morgue"}
  </choice>
  <choice id="thirteen" label="Drawer 13" when="entry.bedCard.read">
    @narrator{code="0040"}: Tobias. Blue at the lips, a hospital band on his wrist in handwriting from 1979.
    @nell{code="0020" emotion="afraid"}: Toby. Toby, look at me.
    ::retract{taken(tobias)}
    ::assert{following(tobias)}
    ::assert{solved(freezer)}
    @tobias{code="0010"}: ...Nell? They said I had to be in bed by three.
    @nell{code="0030" emotion="relieved"}: You're not in bed. You're with me. Up. Walk.
  </choice>
</branch>
